From: immortalwrt-x86-64-fm350-pcie <noreply@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: wwan: t7xx: rate-limit TX queue full log

The TX full notification can be delivered repeatedly while the modem is
not returning completions.  The unbounded netdev_err() call then floods the
kernel log and obscures the first diagnostic message.

Keep stopping the netdev queue as before, but rate-limit the message.  This
does not change TX queue flow control or the GRO data path.

---
 drivers/net/wwan/t7xx/t7xx_netdev.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wwan/t7xx/t7xx_netdev.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wwan/t7xx/t7xx_netdev.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #include <linux/ip.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/list.h>
+#include <linux/net.h>
 #include <linux/netdev_features.h>
 #include <linux/netdevice.h>
 #include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
@@ -451,7 +452,8 @@ static void t7xx_ccmni_queue_tx_full_notify(struct t7xx_ccmni_ctrl *ctlb, int qno)
 	struct netdev_queue *net_queue;
 
 	if (atomic_read(&ccmni->usage) > 0) {
-		netdev_err(ccmni->dev, "TX queue %d is full\n", qno);
+		if (net_ratelimit())
+			netdev_err(ccmni->dev, "TX queue %d is full\n", qno);
 		net_queue = netdev_get_tx_queue(ccmni->dev, qno);
 		netif_tx_stop_queue(net_queue);
 	}
